I challenge catalogue row [9c839bd675122bb9] which claims the response-verdict kernel does not move under upper-case. The row's example likely lacks JSON boolean literals. My input contains the JSON literal `true` as a value. The upper-case transform converts `true` to `TRUE`, which is not valid JSON (only lowercase `true`, `false`, `null` are valid literals). Before the transform, strict parsing succeeds and the verdict is JSON_OBJECT. After the transform, strict parsing fails on `TRUE`, recovery also fails (the decoder rejects `TRUE`), and no refusal phrase is present, so the verdict becomes INVALID_JSON. This refutes the 'moves: false' claim.
